 "max_turns": 60,
 "prompt": "This directory holds ldiff, a line-based diff and patch tool: the package ldiff/ (line model, alignment, hunks, unified-diff writer, patch parser, hunk locator, patch applier, command line) with run.py as the command (`python3 run.py diff OLD NEW`, `python3 run.py patch FILE PATCHFILE`, `python3 run.py stat PATCHFILE`). It does not behave as SPEC.md describes: some of the examples in examples/ give the wrong result (`python3 run_examples.py` runs them all and compares the output and the written files with the expected ones). Fix the implementation so that it follows SPEC.md in every respect; more tests than the visible examples check the whole of SPEC.md. Do not modify SPEC.md, run_examples.py or anything in examples/. Code must run on /usr/bin/python3 (Python 3.9), the interpreter the checks use; standard library only.",
